-- title:
--   Divisor specialisation on X₀(N) preserves degree zero and principality
-- statement:
--   Fix a nonzero natural number $N$, a prime $\ell$ and a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ whose residue field $k_A = A/\mathfrak{m}_A$ has characteristic $\ell$, and assume $\ell \nmid N$. Let $fm$ be a fibre model of level $N$ over $A$ in characteristic $\ell$ with reduction map the residue map $A \to k_A$: that is, a pair of subrings $B_{\mathrm{fin}}, B_{\mathrm{inf}}$ of the base change to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of the full level-$N$ modular function field inside Laurent series, each containing the image of $A$ under the constants homomorphism, with $\bar j$ and $\bar j_N$ in $B_{\mathrm{fin}}$ and $\bar j^{-1}$ in $B_{\mathrm{inf}}$, each integral over the corresponding affine chart base generated by the constants together with $\bar j$ (resp. $\bar j^{-1}$), and equipped with ring homomorphisms $\pi_{\mathrm{fin}}, \pi_{\mathrm{inf}}$ to the level-$N$ modular function field over $k_A$ sending constants to their residues and $\bar j, \bar j_N, \bar j^{-1}$ to their characteristic-$\ell$ counterparts. Assume furthermore a cusp chart $cc$ for $fm$, namely that $\bar j_N \cdot (\bar j^{-1})^N$ lies in $B_{\mathrm{inf}}$ and that $\pi_{\mathrm{inf}}$ sends it to $j_N \cdot j^{-N}$ over $k_A$; modular polynomial data $\Phi_d \in \mathbb{Z}[X][Y]$ (monic of degree $\psi(d)$ in $Y$ and vanishing at $(j, j(q^d))$) for every divisor $d$ of $N$; and that the image of $\Phi_N$ in $k_A(X)[Y]$ is separable. Then the divisor specialisation map $\mathrm{sp}_*$ attached to $fm$, with surjectivity of the residue map supplied by surjectivity of the quotient map, satisfies both clauses of `SpDivPreservesPrincipal`: every divisor $D$ of the modular function field over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lying in the kernel of the degree map has $\mathrm{sp}_* D$ again of degree zero, and if such a $D$ is moreover principal, i.e. $D = \sum_v \mathrm{ord}_v(f)\, v$ for some nonzero function $f$, then $\mathrm{sp}_* D$ is principal in the divisor group of the level-$N$ modular function field over $k_A$.
--
--   This is the statement that, for level prime to the residue characteristic, the specialisation of divisors along a fibre model of $X_0(N)$ descends to the degree-zero and to the principal subgroups, the first step towards specialisation of the divisor class group in good reduction. It is used in the construction of fibre models with cusp charts whose specialisation of places agrees with the place-level map, and in the production of prolongation tuples that are models with the order law fixed.
